//3862. Find the Smallest Balanced Index
//Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/find-the-smallest-balanced-index/
# Intuition: 
We need an index i where sum of left elements = product of right elements.

Instead of recalculating the product every time, we precompute suffix products so the right product can be obtained in O(1).

While scanning the array, we maintain a running prefix sum (leftSum).

Since products grow exponentially and sums grow linearly, the product can overflow long.

So we cap the suffix product at 1e14, because any value larger than that can never equal the prefix sum.

For each index, compare leftSum with suffixProduct[i+1]; if equal, that index is the smallest balanced index.
TC = O(n)
SC = O(n)


class Solution {
    public int smallestBalancedIndex(int[] nums) {
        int n=nums.length;
        long suffProd[]=new long[n];
        suffProd[n-1]=nums[n-1];
        for(int i=n-2;i>=0;i--){
             if (suffProd[i + 1] > 1e14) {
                suffProd[i] = (long)1e14 + 1; // cap value
            } else {
                suffProd[i] = nums[i] * suffProd[i + 1];
                if (suffProd[i] > 1e14) suffProd[i] = (long)1e14 + 1;
            }
        }
        long leftSum=0;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            long rightProd=1;
            if(i+1<n)rightProd=suffProd[i+1];
            if(leftSum>1e14)return -1;
            if(leftSum==rightProd)return i;
            leftSum+=nums[i];
        }
    return -1;
    }
}
